Hi everyone. I'm not sure if this the place for a question this simple, but 
here goes:

I'm just learning the very basics of Lojban, and I'm now trying to actually 
express some simple ideas with the grammar/vocabulary I have, in order to 
check my grasp of the concepts. Of course, it's hard for me to be sure I am 
doing this correctly. That said, will anyone tell me if I'm saying the 
phrase "I love my family" correctly in Lojban? I came up with: "prami le mi 
lanzu fa mi". I'm obviously trying to play around with place structure. I 
thought this form had a nice ring to it, versus the simpler "mi prami le mi 
lanzu.

Thanks for your time/interest!

